***************************** T A L Y S **************************1525 1451  194
                                                                  1525 1451  195
TALYS is a computer code system for the prediction and analysis   1525 1451  196
of nuclear reactions. TALYS simulates reactions that involve      1525 1451  197
neutrons, gamma-rays, protons, deuterons, tritons, helions and    1525 1451  198
alpha-particles, in the 1 keV - 200 MeV energy range. This is     1525 1451  199
achieved by implementing a suite of nuclear reaction models into  1525 1451  200
a single code system. This nuclear data file is based on a        1525 1451  201
theoretical analysis that utilizes the optical model, compound    1525 1451  202
nucleus statistical theory, fission, direct reactions and         1525 1451  203
pre-equilibrium processes, in combination with databases and      1525 1451  204
models for nuclear structure. The following output of TALYS is    1525 1451  205
stored in this data file:                                         1525 1451  206
                                                                  1525 1451  207
- Total, elastic and non-elastic cross sections                   1525 1451  208
- Inelastic cross sections to discrete states                     1525 1451  209
- Exclusive channel cross sections, e.g. (n,g), (n,2n), (n,np),.. 1525 1451  210
- Inelastic scattering angular distributions to discrete states   1525 1451  211
- Exclusive channel energy spectra                                1525 1451  212
- Exclusive channel double-differential spectra                   1525 1451  213
- Exclusive gamma production for discrete states and continuum    1525 1451  214
- Elastic scattering angular distributions                        1525 1451  215
- Recoil data                                                     1525 1451  216
- Total particle cross sections, e.g. (n,xn), (n,xp),..           1525 1451  217
- Total particle energy spectra                                   1525 1451  218
- Total particle double-differential spectra                      1525 1451  219
- Isomeric and ground state cross sections                        1525 1451  220
- Residual production cross sections                              1525 1451  221
                                                                  1525 1451  222
For a description of the used nuclear models and their            1525 1451  223
parameterization we refer to [kon19]. If for this specific        1525 1451  224
nuclide we deviate from the global parameterization, it is made   1525 1451  225
explicit above under Nuclide Specific Information.                1525 1451  226
                                                                  1525 1451  227
***************** F I L E   I N F O R M A T I O N ****************1525 1451  228
